Experiment No.: 9

Title

Demonstration of I2C Communication Protocol

Aim

To demonstrate I2C communication between Arduino devices.

Theory

I2C (Inter-Integrated Circuit) is a serial communication protocol that uses two wires: SDA (Serial Data) and SCL (Serial Clock). It allows multiple devices to communicate using the same bus.

Components Required
Arduino Uno
Jumper Wires
USB Cable
Computer/Laptop
Procedure
Connect Arduino Uno to the computer.
Connect SDA and SCL pins for I2C communication.
Include the Wire library in the program.
Upload the program.
Observe the data transmission.
Code
#include <Wire.h>

void setup()
{
  Wire.begin();
  Serial.begin(9600);
}

void loop()
{
  Wire.beginTransmission(8);
  Wire.write("Hello");
  Wire.endTransmission();

  Serial.println("Data Sent");
  delay(1000);
}
